Helios DXVK fork: the no-event scanout-acquire signaler idles when nothing is armed

Conduit guest/windows. Applied after 0015 by ci/windows/Build-Driver.ps1.

The signaler thread starts on the first armed gate and runs until the device
is destroyed. Without a retirement event it polls the read ledger every 1 ms
holding timeBeginPeriod(1), also when no gate is armed, so a refused device
that armed once keeps the process at a 1 ms timer period and 1000 wakeups/s
for as long as it lives.

After about 100 ms of polls with no gate armed it now polls every 10 ms and
gives the 1 ms period back; armFence wakes it, and the next armed gate polls
at 1 ms again. winmm is resolved once per thread instead of on every
timeBeginPeriod. The event path is unchanged.

